      "side": 1,
      "message": "Half done in patch set 3.\n\nThe first problem is fixed: a heap that was full and has been emptied still interns, and `an_emptied_heap_is_not_refused_for_its_pages` covers it.\n\nThe second is fixed in one order only. When symbols are charged first, later pages are refused in time, as `the_heap_stops_growing_where_the_charges_leave_no_room` checks. When the heap takes its pages first, `charge_external` compares the charges alone with the limit, so they can add nearly another `max_bytes` on top of pages the heap never gives back. Probe, appended to `crates/vali-runtime/tests/it/limits.rs` on 1260691 patch set 3:\n\n```\nlet limit \u003d vali_runtime::PAGE_BYTES * 8;\nlet mut cx \u003d Cx::\u003cS\u003e::new(\u0026HeapConfig { max_bytes: Some(limit), ..Default::default() });\ndrop(fill(\u0026mut cx));\ncx.collect_garbage();\nlet name \u003d \"n\".repeat(1000);\nlet mut made \u003d 0;\nwhile cx.symbol(\u0026format!(\"{name}{made}\")).is_ok() { made +\u003d 1; }\n// cx.bytes_used() + made * name.len() vs limit\n```\n\nUnder all four counting strategies the result is 262,144 bytes of pages plus at least 186,000 bytes of name charges (186 symbols), 1.71 times the limit. It then fails with `OutOfMemory` because the heap itself runs out of room for the names\u0027 strings, not because of the charge check.\n\nSuggested fix: when a charge doesn\u0027t fit next to the pages, have the page heap give empty pages back to the source first, then check `used + external` on every charge as on every page. `PageSource::free_large` already frees any block by its recorded layout, and `PageHeap::free` already puts a page with no live blocks on the empty list. An emptied heap would still intern, because its empty pages go back to make room, and pages plus charges would stay under the limit in both orders. A test for this order would go next to the two above.",
